{"cuisine/ancient-roman-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/ancient-roman-cuisine","n":"Ancient Roman cuisine","c":"#a99fb5","crumb":[["Cuisine"]],"sub":"Historical cuisine","intro":[["The cuisine of ancient Rome changed significantly over the duration of the civilization's existence. Dietary habits were affected by the political changes from kingdom to republic to empire, and Roman trading with foreigners along with the empire's enormous expansion exposed Romans to many new foods, provincial culinary habits and cooking methods."],["In the beginning, dietary differences between Roman social classes were not great, but disparities developed with the empire's growth."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ancient-roman-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Roman_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Pass the Garum","ref":"site/pass-the-garum-blogspot-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pass-the-garum.blogspot.com","note":"Blog by an ancient history graduate recreating Roman recipes as closely as possible to the sources; may no longer be updated.","url":"https://pass-the-garum.blogspot.com/p/about-me.html","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":3,"rows":[{"name":"Cooking Apicius: Roman Recipes for Today","ref":"cookbook/cooking-apicius-roman-recipes-for-today","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Sally Grainger","note":"Classicist and cook Sally Grainger's tested modern versions of recipes from the Roman Apicius collection, from Prospect Books.","url":"https://prospectbooks.co.uk/products-page/current-titles/cooking-apicius","suggested":true},{"name":"The Classical Cookbook (revised edition)","ref":"cookbook/the-classical-cookbook-revised-edition","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Andrew Dalby and Sally Grainger, 2012","note":"Getty Publications book of Greek and Roman recipes adapted from ancient texts by two food historians.","url":"https://shop.getty.edu/product