-bite"],["Boiling Springs Tavern","dish/boiling-springs-tavern"],["Brix Tavern","dish/brix-tavern"],["Brown Betty (dessert)","dish/brown-betty-dessert"],["Brown Derby","dish/brown-derby"],["Brunswick stew","dish/brunswick-stew"],["Buffalo wing","dish/buffalo-wing"],["Buona","dish/buona"],["Busboys and Poets","dish/busboys-and-poets"],["Butter cake","dish/butter-cake"],["Byways Cafe","dish/byways-cafe"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["California Grill","dish/california-grill"],["Camp Washington Chili","dish/camp-washington-chili"],["Caramel apple","dish/caramel-apple"],["Carbonara","dish/carbonara"],["Carnation Cafe","dish/carnation-cafe"],["Cheesesteak","dish/cheesesteak"],["Chicago-style hot dog","dish/chicago-style-hot-dog"],["Chicken nugget","dish/chicken-nugget"],["Chiffon cake","dish/chiffon-cake"],["Chili con carne","dish/chili-con-carne"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/4/4d/Grasshopper_pie_%2814105460720%29.jpg/500px-Grasshopper_pie_%2814105460720%29.jpg","w":500,"h":425,"by":"Julia Payne from Manchester, USA","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grasshopper_pie_(14105460720).jpg"}},"dish/kue-gapit":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/kue-gapit","n":"Kue gapit","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indonesian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Kue gapit is an Indonesian kue kering (dry snack) which originates from Cirebon, West Java. Generally made from tapioca flour, its name comes from the cooking process, in which it is grilled between iron molds like a waffle. The snack comes in a variety of shapes and flavors. Though it is a popular souvenir among visitors to Cirebon, residents of the region rarely eat it."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-kue-gapit"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kue_gapit"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"